    <string name="description">Description</string>
    <string name="ex_description_generic">Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Execute the movement with a controlled tempo and a full range of motion while strictly engaging the %1$s.</string>
    <string name="ex_bench_press_desc">Lie on your back. Lower the weight to your mid-chest, then press up until arms are fully extended.</string>
    <string name="ex_squats_desc">Stand with feet shoulder-width apart. Lower your hips as if sitting in a chair, then drive back up to standing.</string>
    <string name="ex_deadlifts_desc">Hinge at hips to grip the bar. Keeping a flat back, drive through your heels to stand up straight.</string>
    <string name="ex_pull_ups_desc">Hang from a bar and pull your chest toward it by driving your elbows down. Lower yourself with control.</string>
    <string name="ex_overhead_press_desc">Press the weight from shoulder level upward until arms are locked out. Keep your core tight.</string>
    <string name="ex_curls">Curls</string>
    <string name="ex_curls_desc">Keep elbows close to your sides. Curl the weights toward your shoulders, then lower slowly.</string>
    <string name="ex_rows_desc">Hinge forward with a flat back. Pull the weight toward your lower ribs, squeezing your shoulder blades.</string>
    <string name="ex_lateral_raise_desc">Raise weights out to your sides until arms are level with shoulders. Keep a slight bend in your elbows.</string>
    <string name="ex_plank_desc">Support weight on forearms and toes. Keep your body in a straight line; do not let your hips sag.</string>
    <string name="ex_tricep_extension_desc">Lower the weight behind your head by bending elbows, then straighten arms to press the weight back up.</string>
    <string name="ex_lunges_desc">Step forward and lower your hips until both knees are bent at 90 degrees. Push back up to the start.</string>
    <string name="ex_crunches_desc">Lift your shoulders off the floor while pressing your lower back firmly into the mat.</string>
    <string name="ex_leg_raises_desc">Lift your straight legs toward the ceiling and lower them slowly with control.</string>
    <string name="ex_abs_desc">For crunches, lift shoulders off the floor. For leg raises, lift straight legs from the floor toward the ceiling.</string>
    <string name="ex_flyes_desc">Lie on a bench with a slight bend in your elbows. Lower the weights out to your sides in an arc, then squeeze your chest to bring them back together.</string>
    <string name="ex_shrugs_desc">Hold weights at your sides with arms straight. Elevate your shoulders toward your ears, pause at the top, then lower slowly.</string>
    <string name="ex_face_pulls_desc">Using a rope or cable, pull toward your face keeping elbows high. Focus on squeezing your rear delts and upper back.</string>
    <string name="ex_back_extensions_desc">Hinge at the hips to lower your upper body, then use your lower back and glutes to raise yourself back to neutral.</string>
    <string name="ex_woodchoppers_desc">Using a cable or weight, pull diagonally across your body while rotating your core. Move from high to low or low to high.</string>
    <string name="ex_push_ups_desc">Maintain a straight line from head to heels. Lower your chest toward the floor, then push back up by extending your arms.</string>
    <string name="ex_dips_desc">Lower your body by bending your elbows until your shoulders are at 90 degrees, then push back up to the starting position.</string>
    <string name="ex_leg_curls_desc">Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending your knees, then lower the weight slowly with control.</string>
    <string name="ex_leg_press_desc">Push the platform away by extending your knees and hips, then lower it back down with control without locking your knees.</string>
    <string name="ex_calf_raises_desc">Rise up onto the balls of your feet as high as possible, pause at the top, then lower your heels below the starting position.</string>
    <string name="ex_side_lying_leg_raise_desc">Lie on your side with legs straight. Lift your top leg toward the ceiling while keeping it straight, then lower slowly.</string>

    <string name="ex_incline_press_desc">Lie on an incline bench. Press the weights upward from your upper chest until arms are extended, then lower with control.</string>
    <string name="ex_decline_press_desc">Lie on a decline bench. Press the weights upward from your lower chest until arms are extended, then lower with control.</string>
    <string name="ex_lat_pulldown_desc">Pull the bar down toward your upper chest by driving your elbows down and back. Squeeze your lats at the bottom.</string>
    <string name="ex_seated_row_desc">Pull the handle toward your lower stomach while keeping your back straight. Squeeze your shoulder blades together.</string>
    <string name="ex_shoulder_press_desc">Press the weights from shoulder level upward until arms are locked out. Keep your core tight and back straight.</string>
    <string name="ex_front_raise_desc">Raise the weights directly in front of you until arms are level with shoulders. Avoid swinging your body.</string>
    <string name="ex_side_raise_desc">Raise the weights out to your sides until arms are level with shoulders. Keep a slight bend in your elbows.</string>
    <string name="ex_bicep_curl_desc">Curl the weights toward your shoulders while keeping your elbows pinned to your sides. Lower slowly.</string>
    <string name="ex_hammer_curl_desc">Curl the weights with a neutral grip (palms facing each other). Maintain control throughout the movement.</string>
    <string name="ex_tricep_pushdown_desc">Push the bar or rope down until your arms are fully extended. Keep your elbows stationary at your sides.</string>
    <string name="ex_leg_extension_desc">Extend your legs until they are straight, focusing on the contraction in your quadriceps. Lower with control.</string>
    <string name="ex_leg_curl_desc">Curl your heels toward your glutes. Squeeze your hamstrings at the peak and lower slowly.</string>
    <string name="ex_goblet_squat_desc">Hold a weight at chest height. Squat down deep while keeping your chest up and back flat.</string>
    <string name="ex_romanian_deadlift_desc">Hinge at the hips with a slight knee bend. Lower the weight along your legs until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings.</string>
    <string name="ex_russian_twist_desc">Rotate your torso from side to side while sitting with knees bent. Touch the floor or hold a weight for intensity.</string>
    <string name="ex_cable_crunch_desc">Kneel and pull the rope down by crunching your abs toward your knees. Keep your hips stationary.</string>

    <string name="ex_bird_dog_desc">Start on all fours. Extend the opposite arm and leg simultaneously while keeping your back flat and core engaged.</string>
    <string name="ex_pullover_desc">Lie on your back. Hold the weight with both hands and lower it behind your head in an arc, then pull it back over your chest.</string>
    <string name="ex_superman_desc">Lie face down on the floor. Simultaneously lift your arms, chest, and legs off the ground, then lower them slowly.</string>
    <string name="ex_good_morning_desc">With a weight on your upper back or at chest height, hinge forward at the hips while keeping your back straight and knees slightly bent.</string>
    <string name="ex_mountain_climbers_desc">In a plank position, drive your knees toward your chest one at a time in a quick, alternating motion.</string>
    <string name="ex_hollow_hold_desc">Lie on your back and lift your legs and shoulders off the floor, pressing your lower back firmly into the ground.</string>
    <string name="ex_clamshell_desc">Lie on your side with knees bent. Lift your top knee while keeping your feet together, focusing on your side glutes.</string>

