    <string name="ex_hip_thrust_desc">Drive your hips upward toward the ceiling by squeezing your glutes until your body forms a straight line from knees to shoulders.</string>
    <string name="ex_kickbacks_desc">Extend your arm or leg backward under control, keeping your core stable and squeezing the target muscle at full extension.</string>
    <string name="ex_pulldown_desc">Pull the bar down toward your upper chest by driving your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats at the bottom.</string>
    <string name="ex_carry_desc">Hold the weight with a tall posture and braced core, taking steady, controlled steps while maintaining shoulder stability.</string>
    <string name="ex_rollout_desc">Roll forward while keeping your core tight and lower back flat, then contract your abs to pull yourself back to the start.</string>
    <string name="ex_explosive_desc">Explode upward through your hips and legs to drive the weight overhead or to shoulder height in one continuous motion.</string>

    <string name="ex_desc_fallback_chest">Contract your chest to press or move the weight forward, maintaining stable shoulders and controlling the stretch.</string>
    <string name="ex_desc_fallback_back">Drive your elbows backward and squeeze your shoulder blades together to pull the weight toward your torso.</string>
    <string name="ex_desc_fallback_shoulders">Press or raise the weight using your shoulder muscles, keeping your core braced and avoiding excessive momentum.</string>
    <string name="ex_desc_fallback_legs">Drive through your feet to extend your knees and hips, keeping your chest up and knees aligned with your toes.</string>
    <string name="ex_desc_fallback_biceps">Keep your elbows close to your torso and bend at the elbow joint to curl the weight upward with control.</string>
    <string name="ex_desc_fallback_triceps">Extend at the elbow joint to push the weight straight, focusing on squeezing your triceps at full lockout.</string>
    <string name="ex_desc_fallback_abs">Brace your midsection and flex or rotate your torso under control, focusing on contracting your abdominals.</string>
    <string name="ex_desc_fallback_generic">Perform the movement with precision. Control the weight throughout the entire path and focus on the maximum contraction of your %1$s.</string>

